{
	"Name": "AlertQuery - Okta - User - Session - Multiple Okta Sessions Detected for a Single User [table]",
	"Description": "Finds accounts running several concurrent Okta sessions from several source addresses. One person on a laptop and a phone is normal and shows up as two sessions from one or two addresses; an account shared with an adversary shows more sessions from more addresses.\n\nThresholds: 3 or more distinct external session IDs and 2 or more distinct source addresses. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune them.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_multiple_sessions_detected_for_single_user/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/tree/master/rules/identity/okta",
	"GUID": "cd334285-a6f7-5a99-a44f-1ab1f2c542e1",
	"Labels": [
